# ---- docs ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `docs/` can no longer be excluded wholesale: the `docs-build` stage runs Sphinx over it, and an
# excluded path is simply absent from the context, so `COPY docs/requirements.txt` copied nothing
# and pip failed with "Could not open requirements file" — a missing *file* error for what is
# really a missing *context*.
#
# The docs still never reach the image as source. The final stage copies only the built HTML
# (`COPY --from=docs-build /build/static/docs/`), so this widens the build context and not the
# shipped artifact.
#
# What stays out is the 2.9 MB Sphinx does not read: `conf.py` already excludes `screenshots` and
# the operational runbooks (`[A-Z]*.md`), so shipping them into the context would cost build time
# and cache invalidation for nothing.
docs/screenshots
docs/_build
docs/*.pdf
docs/*.csv
docs/*.png

*.md

# Built docs, for the same reason `static/spa` is here: the image gets them from `docs-build`, so
# a stale local build must not be copied in by `COPY static/`.
static/docs
.cursor
.env
.env.*
